se cloud scheduler to make our  job run every night  i go to cloud scheduler  create a new job  give it a name and a region to run in  set a schedule for it to run using cron  tab notation  and a time zone  click continue  target type http  enter the cloud run admin api endpoint  to run your job  you can find that in the  documentation and keep http method as  post  now we have to give cloud scheduler  permissions to start the job i click  here to pick oauth token  and then i select which service account  scheduler should use to start the job  i know this one has sufficient  permission  you need a service account that has the  cloud run invoker permission on the job  then i click create  now the job will be run nightly you  won't have to be at your keyboard at  midnight martin  that that's a relief uh  the the code you showed me processed one  invoice at a time in series  if we have a thousand invoices that  would take a long time uh can we speed  it up somehow yes you can tell cloudrun  jobs to start several parallel tasks  let's say you have a thousand invoices  and you start 10 parallel tasks  your code can detect what number task it  is for example 4 out of 10  then your code can process its part of  the total work  for task number four that would be  invoices 301 to 400. sounds very useful  for large jobs  like big old data migration jobs that  need to process millions of records  um do you have a code example for that  let's save that for another video martin  also it's all in the documentation  uh the link is in the description  very good thanks for showing us uh  and thank you everyone for watching if  you have questions for carolina or me  let us know in the comments also let us  know if there are other server-less  topics you'd like to hear about  until next time  [Music]  you
 

